@page "/getting-started"

<PageTitle>Getting Started — SpawnDev.ILGPU.ML</PageTitle>

<div class="gs-page">
    <h1 class="gs-title">Getting Started</h1>
    <p class="gs-intro">
        Add GPU-accelerated ML inference to your .NET app. Same C# runs in Blazor WASM and on desktop —
        WebGPU / WebGL / Wasm in the browser, CUDA / OpenCL / CPU on the desktop. No ONNX Runtime.
    </p>

    <div class="gs-steps">
        <div class="gs-step">
            <div class="step-number">1</div>
            <div class="step-content">
                <h3>Install</h3>
                <div class="code-block">
                    <pre><code>dotnet add package SpawnDev.ILGPU.ML
<span class="cm"># Browser (Blazor WASM) also needs SpawnJS:</span>
dotnet add package SpawnDev.SpawnJS</code></pre>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="gs-step">
            <div class="step-number">2</div>
            <div class="step-content">
                <h3>Create an accelerator</h3>
                <p class="step-desc">
                    <code>MLContext</code> enables Algorithms (required for MathF on CUDA/OpenCL).
                    <code>AllAcceleratorsAsync</code> discovers browser devices; preferred order is
                    WebGPU → WebGL → Wasm in the browser, CUDA → OpenCL → CPU on desktop.
                </p>
                <div class="code-block">
<pre><code><span class="kw">using</span> <span class="ns">SpawnDev.ILGPU.ML</span>;

<span class="kw">var</span> builder = <span class="ty">MLContext</span>.<span class="fn">Create</span>();
<span class="kw">await</span> builder.<span class="fn">AllAcceleratorsAsync</span>();
<span class="kw">using var</span> context = builder.<span class="fn">ToContext</span>();
<span class="kw">using var</span> accelerator = <span class="kw">await</span> context.<span class="fn">CreatePreferredAcceleratorAsync</span>();</code></pre>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="gs-step">
            <div class="step-number">3</div>
            <div class="step-content">
                <h3>Load a model</h3>
                <p class="step-desc">
                    Prefer streaming weights through the hub into OPFS — never materialize a large model as a
                    <code>byte[]</code> on the WASM heap. <code>HubModelSource</code> is the default (plain HTTP + OPFS).
                    <code>CreateFromStreamAsync</code> auto-detects ONNX / GGUF / TFLite / … from magic bytes
                    (same prefix as the Model Inspector). Optional P2P delivery is a separate package:
                    <code>SpawnDev.ILGPU.ML.WebTorrent</code>.
                </p>
                <div class="code-block">
<pre><code><span class="kw">using</span> <span class="ns">SpawnDev.ILGPU.ML</span>;
<span class="kw">using</span> <span class="ns">SpawnDev.ILGPU.ML.Hub</span>;

<span class="cm">// Browser path (preferred): stream from hub → OPFS → GPU (format auto-detected)</span>
<span class="kw">using var</span> source = <span class="kw">new</span> <span class="ty">HubModelSource</span>(JS);   <span class="cm">// or inject as a singleton</span>
<span class="kw">await using var</span> stream = <span class="kw">await</span> source.<span class="fn">OpenAsync</span>(
    <span class="ty">ModelHub</span>.<span class="ty">KnownModels</span>.SqueezeNet, <span class="st">"squeezenet1.1-7.onnx"</span>);
<span class="kw">var</span> session = <span class="kw">await</span> <span class="ty">InferenceSession</span>.<span class="fn">CreateFromStreamAsync</span>(accelerator, stream);

<span class="cm">// Convenience wrapper (same delivery under the hood; needs the filename):</span>
<span class="kw">using var</span> hub = <span class="kw">new</span> <span class="ty">ModelHub</span>(JS);
<span class="kw">var</span> session2 = <span class="kw">await</span> <span class="ty">InferenceSession</span>.<span class="fn">CreateFromHuggingFaceAsync</span>(
    accelerator, hub, <span class="ty">ModelHub</span>.<span class="ty">KnownModels</span>.SqueezeNet, <span class="st">"squeezenet1.1-7.onnx"</span>);

<span class="cm">// Desktop / small files: URL through the hub (CORS + cache). Avoid for large browser weights.</span>
<span class="kw">var</span> url = <span class="ty">HuggingFaceClient</span>.<span class="fn">GetDownloadUrl</span>(
    <span class="ty">ModelHub</span>.<span class="ty">KnownModels</span>.SqueezeNet, <span class="st">"squeezenet1.1-7.onnx"</span>);
<span class="kw">var</span> session3 = <span class="kw">await</span> <span class="ty">InferenceSession</span>.<span class="fn">CreateFromFileAsync</span>(accelerator, httpClient, url);</code></pre>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="gs-step">
            <div class="step-number">4</div>
            <div class="step-content">
                <h3>Run inference</h3>
                <p class="step-desc">Create a pipeline, feed it data, get results. All on GPU.</p>
                <div class="code-block">
<pre><code><span class="kw">using</span> <span class="ns">SpawnDev.ILGPU.ML.Pipelines</span>;

<span class="kw">var</span> pipeline = <span class="kw">new</span> <span class="ty">ClassificationPipeline</span>(session, accelerator);
<span class="kw">var</span> results = <span class="kw">await</span> pipeline.<span class="fn">ClassifyAsync</span>(rgbaPixels, width, height);

<span class="kw">foreach</span> (<span class="kw">var</span> r <span class="kw">in</span> results)
    Console.<span class="fn">WriteLine</span>(<span class="st">$"</span>{r.Label}: {r.Confidence:P1}<span class="st">"</span>);
<span class="cm">// e.g. tiger cat: 52.0%</span></code></pre>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="gs-step">
            <div class="step-number">5</div>
            <div class="step-content">
                <h3>Inspect a model</h3>
                <p class="step-desc">
                    Check structure and operator compatibility before loading. Prefer the
                    <a href="inspector">Model Inspector</a> demo for large files (streaming, structure-only).
                </p>
                <div class="code-block">
<pre><code><span class="kw">using</span> <span class="ns">SpawnDev.ILGPU.ML.Onnx</span>;

<span class="cm">// Small models only — materializes the whole byte[] on the managed heap</span>
<span class="kw">var</span> summary = <span class="ty">OnnxLoader</span>.<span class="fn">GetModelSummary</span>(onnxBytes);
<span class="kw">var</span> compat = <span class="ty">ModelInspectorHelper</span>.<span class="fn">CheckCompatibility</span>(onnxBytes);
<span class="cm">// compat.IsFullyCompatible / compat.SupportedOps / …</span></code></pre>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="gs-section">
        <h2>Blazor WASM setup</h2>
        <p>
            Register SpawnJS in <code>Program.cs</code> (<code>builder.Services.AddSpawnJSRuntime(...)</code>).
            ILGPU needs IL reflection at runtime — keep trimming and AOT off:
        </p>
        <div class="code-block">
<pre><code><span class="cm">&lt;!-- In your .csproj — required for ILGPU --&gt;</span>
<span class="tag">&lt;PropertyGroup&gt;</span>
    <span class="tag">&lt;PublishTrimmed&gt;</span>false<span class="tag">&lt;/PublishTrimmed&gt;</span>
    <span class="tag">&lt;RunAOTCompilation&gt;</span>false<span class="tag">&lt;/RunAOTCompilation&gt;</span>
<span class="tag">&lt;/PropertyGroup&gt;</span></code></pre>
        </div>
    </div>

